                mechanism: "Comets and the ice-rich small bodies past the frost line carry exactly what is missing: water, CO2, and ammonia, which is both a strong greenhouse gas and the nitrogen source needed later. Delivery is gravity assists rather than propulsion, because a small nudge at the right point in an orbit converts into an enormous change over decades of free flight. Each impact also deposits its kinetic energy as heat, so the delivery and the warming are the same event. The cost is measured in objects rather than in joules, and the number of objects is the honest headline.",
