                mechanism: "A breathable atmosphere is mostly the gas you do not breathe. Oxygen at its sea-level partial pressure in a pure-oxygen atmosphere is chemically the same for a lung and catastrophically different for everything else: flame spread rates rise by orders of magnitude, which is what killed the Apollo 1 crew. An inert buffer at roughly four fifths of the total is not a luxury. Nitrogen is the only candidate available in quantity, and the outer system supplies it as ammonia, which doubles as greenhouse forcing on the way in.",
                quantities: [
