            TerraformStep(
                order: 5,
                title: "Oxygenate it, which is the slow step",
                mechanism: "Oxygen has to be prised out of CO2 or out of metal oxides, and both are strongly uphill: splitting a mole of CO2 costs 257 kilojoules, and no catalyst changes a thermodynamic floor. Doing it industrially means finding that energy. Doing it biologically means photosynthesis, which is the same reaction powered by sunlight at about one per cent efficiency, and which is how Earth did it. Earth's own Great Oxidation took hundreds of millions of years, and the only reason a terraformed planet would be faster is that it starts with an engineered biosphere rather than with cyanobacteria inventing the chemistry from scratch.",
