            ),
            TerraformStep(
                order: 2,
                title: "Float, and check which way the buoyancy points",
                mechanism: "A habitat at ambient pressure floats or sinks purely on the ratio of molar masses, because at equal pressure and temperature density goes as molar mass and nothing else. This is where the giants and Venus part company, and the sign of one number decides it. Venus's atmosphere is CO2 at 44 g per mole, so breathing air at 29 floats in it and a habitat is a balloon full of air. A gas giant's atmosphere is hydrogen and helium at about 2.3, so breathing air is more than ten times denser than its surroundings and sinks like a stone. A habitat here must be a hot-air balloon of the ambient hydrogen, heated by its own waste power, or it must be held up aerodynamically, and both are far harder than floating.",
