                source: "Palaszewski 2006, NASA/TM-2006-214122 (atmospheric mining of the outer planets)"
            )
        ],
        caveats: [
            "This body emits more heat than it absorbs from the Sun, because it is still contracting. The 102 K here is what sunlight alone would give; published equilibrium temperatures for the giants are higher because they fold that internal flux in, and Jupiter's is 1.67 times its absorbed sunlight.",
            "Every step past the first is an extrapolation from physics that is itself well established. The physics is not in doubt; the engineering has never been attempted at any scale."
