        ladder: [
            TerraformStep(
                order: 1,
                title: "Accept that an open-air surface is off the table, and say why",
                mechanism: "This is the step that decides the whole approach, and it is decided by one number. The Jeans parameter for nitrogen says how tightly this body could hold an atmosphere if one were given to it, and where it falls short, an atmosphere is not a thing you build once but a thing you continuously replace. Where the body is also airless today, there is a second and more immediate problem: no atmosphere means no shielding, and no shielding means the dose at the surface is set by the unattenuated cosmic-ray flux. Both point the same way. The habitat is a sealed volume, and the planet is a place to put it and a source of material, not an environment.",
