                order: 1,
                title: "Start from the two things that are already solved",
                mechanism: "Almost everywhere else on this list, pressure and radiation are the hard problems, and here both are already done. The surface pressure is higher than Earth's, which means a person outside needs warmth and oxygen but not a pressure suit, and a tear in a garment is an inconvenience rather than an emergency. The atmosphere is mostly nitrogen, the same inert buffer that Mars has to import across the solar system. And the column density overhead, together with orbiting inside Saturn's magnetosphere, makes the surface radiation environment mild. Nothing else beyond Mars starts from here.",
                quantities: [
